    <statement><p>Evaluate the line integral
<m>\int_C y\, dx + x\, dy</m> where <m>C</m>
is the parameterized path <m>x = t^{3}</m>, <m>y=t^{2}</m>,
<m>3\le t \le 8</m>.</p>
<p><m>\int_C y\, dx + x\, dy =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8^{5}-3^{5}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>x=t^{3}</m> and <m>y=t^{2}</m> we get <m>dx = 3t^{2}\,dt</m> and
<m>dy = 2t\,dt</m>.  Hence
<me>\int_C y\,dx + x\,dy =
\int_{3}^{8}  t^{2} (3t^{2})\, dt + t^{2} (3t^{2})\, dt =
\int_{3}^{8}  5\,t^4\, dt = (8)^5 - (3)^5 = 32525.</me>




</solution>
